{:edb/db-before-t 1382 :edb/db-after-t 1383 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534695 50 #inst "2026-10-12T08:03:40.384Z" 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186128053 1078 #edb/ref 17592186128058 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186128059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128060 13194139534695 17592186045417 false] [17592186128059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186128062 13194139534695 17592186045417 false] [17592186128059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433093 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186128059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433105 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186128059 1078 #edb/ref 17592186128063 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129206 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433113 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129207 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433111 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129762 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129762 1074 "![](images/d0/d00feacd712c1ca185a8975e8b6343f9937f254631614242003f1d76c1427ffe.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+y-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/59/59b7304dcc07ac38c093b7d8d29d4b4079f192cd9fd0385db9f1981e4640eceb.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+y-z\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y-z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2+y-z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2+y-z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2+y)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2+y)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2+2y\\,dy \\\\  & =[2y+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(2(3)+{3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129763 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129763 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\}.\n$$" 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186129763 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n$R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le π,-2 \\le y \\le 2, 0 \\le z \\le \\sin x}$." 13194139534695 17592186045417 false] [17592186129763 1074 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x[y]_{y=-2}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(2-(-2))\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =-4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(-1-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186235284 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433112 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186433090 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433114 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186433090 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433115 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186433090 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433116 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186433090 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433117 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [17592186433090 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433118 13194139534695 17592186045417 true] [1759